		<!-- Comprehensive SEO Text Section -->
		<div class="mb-16">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 mb-5">Understanding US Visa Processing Times</h2>
			<div class="prose prose-stone max-w-3xl text-stone-600 space-y-5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
				<p>
					Navigating the US immigration system can be an uncertain experience. Whether you are a skilled professional applying for an H-1B visa, an applicant awaiting your Green Card through the I-485 Adjustment of Status, or a permanent resident ready to apply for US Citizenship with the N-400 form, understanding <strong>USCIS processing times</strong> is important to planning your timeline.
				</p>
				<p>
					EasyVisaCheck aggregates data directly from official US government sources, including the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and the US State Department. Our goal is to provide a clear, reliable platform where immigrants, expats, and legal professionals can view both current wait times and historical trends without navigating dense bureaucratic portals.
				</p>
				<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3">How the Visa Bulletin Works</h3>
				<p>
					For individuals in the employment-based (EB) and family-sponsored immigration queues, the monthly <strong>Visa Bulletin</strong> is the most important document published by the State Department. It determines priority dates for applicants from backlogged countries like India, China, Mexico, and the Philippines.
				</p>
				<p>
					The bulletin features two charts: the <em>Final Action Dates</em> chart (when a green card can legally be issued) and the <em>Dates for Filing</em> chart (when applicants residing in the US can submit their I-485 applications to USCIS). Our Visa Bulletin tracker presents these charts clearly, with month-over-month movement highlighted so you can track your priority date progression.
				</p>
				<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3">USCIS Form Processing Variability</h3>
				<p>
					USCIS processing times fluctuate based on application volume, policy changes, and the specific Service Center handling your case.
				</p>
				<p>
					For example, the <strong>Form I-140</strong> (Immigrant Petition for Alien Worker) is the foundational step for employment-based green cards. While Premium Processing guarantees action within 15 business days for a fee, regular processing can take months to over a year. Once the I-140 is approved and your priority date is current, the final step is the <strong>I-485 Adjustment of Status</strong>. Processing times for the I-485 have varied significantly, influenced by interview requirements and background check delays.
				</p>
				<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-3">Why Historical Trends Are Informative</h3>
				<p>
					A single snapshot of current processing times can be misleading. Historical trends reveal whether operations are speeding up or slowing down at specific service centers. We provide trend charts that plot the 80th percentile processing ranges over the past 12–24 months, helping you calibrate expectations without unnecessary alarm.
				</p>
				<p>
					This tool is built strictly on publicly available government data. There are no hidden fees, no required accounts, and no need to hand over sensitive receipt numbers. Just transparent, easy-to-read data to help you understand your US immigration timeline.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- FAQ Section -->
		<div class="mb-8">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-3">
				{faqs.map((faq) => (
					<div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">{faq.question}</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>

	</div>
</Layout>

<script type="application/json" id="search-index-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(searchIndex)} />
<script>
  const data = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('search-index-data')?.textContent || '[]');
  const input = document.getElementById('hero-search-input') as HTMLInputElement;
  const results = document.getElementById('hero-search-results') as HTMLElement;
  const form = document.getElementById('hero-search-form') as HTMLFormElement;

  function render(query: string) {
    if (!query.trim()) {
      results.classList.add('hidden');
      return;
    }
    const q = query.toLowerCase();
    const matches = data.filter((d: any) => d.label.toLowerCase().includes(q)).slice(0, 8);
    if (!matches.length) {
      results.innerHTML = `<div class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-stone-400">No matches — try "H1B", "I-485", or a country name.</div>`;
    } else {
      results.innerHTML = matches.map((m: any) => `
        <a href="${m.href}" class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 hover:bg-stone-50 border-b border-stone-100 last:border-0">
          <span class="text-sm text-stone-800 font-medium">${m.label}</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-400 font-medium">${m.type}</span>
        </a>
      `).join('');
    }
    results.classList.remove('hidden');
  }

  input?.addEventListener('input', () => render(input.value));
  input?.addEventListener('focus', () => render(input.value));
  document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    if (!form.contains(e.target as Node)) results.classList.add('hidden');
  });
  form?.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const first = results.querySelector('a');
    if (first) window.location.href = (first as HTMLAnchorElement).href;
  });
</script>
